Aim:
To draw a human face using Java Applet.

Algorithm:
1. Import the AWT and Applet packages.
2. Create a class named face extending Applet.
3. Use the paint() method to draw the face.
4. Use drawOval(), fillOval(), and fillArc() methods.
5. Display the face.

Program:
import java.awt.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.applet.*;

/*<applet code="face.class" height=300 width=300>
</applet>*/

public class face extends Applet
{
    public void paint(Graphics g)
    {
        g.drawOval(40,40,120,150);
        g.drawOval(57,75,30,20);
        g.drawOval(110,75,30,20);
        g.fillOval(68,81,10,10);
        g.fillOval(121,81,10,10);
        g.fillOval(85,100,30,30);
        g.fillArc(60,125,80,40,180,180);
        g.drawOval(25,92,15,30);
        g.drawOval(160,92,15,30);
    }
}

Output:

A human face is displayed with a head, eyes, pupils, nose, mouth and ears.

Result:

Thus, a human face was drawn successfully using Java Applet.
